{# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Mac health detectors (index=mac_perf, plus the existing os/llm indexes).

   Fed by the macos-wired-memory exec input, which publishes sourcetype
   macos:perf:wired_memory with {"wired_bytes", "wired_ceiling_mb",
   "wired_ceiling_bytes", "wired_ratio", "resident_bytes"}. Thresholds derive
   from observed wired-memory exhaustion on these hosts.

   SOURCETYPE NAMES ARE LOAD-BEARING AND WERE WRONG HERE. Four of the six
   stanzas below shipped asking for sourcetypes that do not exist —
   `macos-wired-memory` (real: macos:perf:wired_memory) and `macos:unifiedlog`
   (real: macos:unified_log). A stanza pointed at a non-existent sourcetype
   returns zero rows on every run forever, which is indistinguishable from
   "all clear", and it does so while enabled with an alert action attached, so
   it looks healthier than a detector that occasionally fires. Take a
   sourcetype from `| tstats count where index=<i> by sourcetype` against the
   live indexer, never from a design document.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------- #}
[mac_wired_ratio_warn]
{{ alert_delivery -}}
description = Warns when a Mac's wired/ceiling ratio (wired_bytes / wired_ceiling_bytes) sustains above 80% for 5 minutes. 80% is chosen to give lead time before the band where exhaustion has been observed, rather than tripping only once already there. VERIFIED BOTH DIRECTIONS 2026-08-23 after the sourcetype fix: the base search now reaches 37 real events (it reached 0 before, by construction); replayed with the condition satisfied it returns 1 row, and with a 0.12 ratio it returns 0. Live ratio on this host is ~0.12, so silence today is the correct answer, not a dark detector.
search = index=mac_perf sourcetype="macos:perf:wired_memory" | stats avg(wired_ratio) as avg_ratio by host | where avg_ratio > 0.80
dispatch.earliest_time = -5m
dispatch.latest_time = now
cron_schedule = */5 * * * *
enableSched = 1
is_visible = 1
disabled = 0
alert.severity = 3
alert.suppress = 1
alert.suppress.period = 30m
alert.suppress.fields = host
alert.track = 1
counttype = number of events
relation = greater than
quantity = 0

[mac_wired_ratio_critical]
{{ alert_delivery -}}
description = Critical: wired/ceiling ratio above 90% sustained for 5 minutes — inside the band where exhaustion has been observed. Same signal as mac_wired_ratio_warn at a higher band so critical pages are distinct from the early warning. VERIFIED BOTH DIRECTIONS 2026-08-23 after the sourcetype fix: replayed at 0.95 it returns 1 row, at 0.85 it returns 0 — so the band boundary is exercised, not just the happy path.
search = index=mac_perf sourcetype="macos:perf:wired_memory" | stats avg(wired_ratio) as avg_ratio by host | where avg_ratio > 0.90
dispatch.earliest_time = -5m
dispatch.latest_time = now
cron_schedule = */5 * * * *
enableSched = 1
is_visible = 1
disabled = 0
alert.severity = 5
alert.suppress = 1
alert.suppress.period = 15m
alert.suppress.fields = host
alert.track = 1
counttype = number of events
relation = greater than
quantity = 0

[mac_leaked_wired_memory]
{{ alert_delivery -}}
description = Detects orphaned wired GPU memory: wired_bytes minus resident_bytes minus the measured ~3.4 GiB non-MLX baseline. 20 GiB is chosen to give lead time roughly halfway to the level at which exhaustion has been observed. VERIFIED BOTH DIRECTIONS 2026-08-23 after the sourcetype fix: replayed with a 38 GiB gap it returns 1 row, with a 2 GiB gap it returns 0.
search = index=mac_perf sourcetype="macos:perf:wired_memory" | eval leaked_gb = round((wired_bytes - resident_bytes - (3.4*1024*1024*1024)) / 1024 / 1024 / 1024, 1) | where leaked_gb > 20
dispatch.earliest_time = -10m
dispatch.latest_time = now
cron_schedule = */10 * * * *
enableSched = 1
is_visible = 1
disabled = 0
alert.severity = 4
alert.suppress = 1
alert.suppress.period = 30m
alert.suppress.fields = host
alert.track = 1
counttype = number of events
relation = greater than
quantity = 0

[mac_metal_oom_burst]
{{ alert_delivery -}}
description = Fires on MLX Metal command-buffer OOM aborts (kIOGPUCommandBufferCallbackErrorOutOfMemory / libc++abi terminating) in index=llm sourcetype=mlx:model-server — a leading indicator of wired-memory exhaustion. VERIFIED by replay against live data: 280 matching events over the trailing 365 days, so the match logic is proven against real history. The trailing `| where count > 0` is load-bearing: a bare `| stats count` emits one row even when nothing matched, and the alert triggers on result rows, so without it this fires every cycle forever.
search = index=llm sourcetype=mlx:model-server ("kIOGPUCommandBufferCallbackErrorOutOfMemory" OR "libc++abi: terminating") | stats count | where count > 0
dispatch.earliest_time = -15m
dispatch.latest_time = now
cron_schedule = */5 * * * *
enableSched = 1
is_visible = 1
disabled = 0
alert.severity = 4
alert.suppress = 1
alert.suppress.period = 30m
alert.track = 1
counttype = number of events
relation = greater than
quantity = 0

[mac_windowserver_watchdog_checkin_gap]
{{ alert_delivery -}}
description = Fires on a "userspace watchdog timeout" line from either the live unified log or a crash-report artifact. VERIFIED BOTH DIRECTIONS against real data: 6 matches over the trailing 365 days (all from macos:crashreport, the .spin artifacts a stall produces) and 0 over the trailing 15 minutes, so it fires on the real signal and is silent when it is absent. Two sources on purpose: the unified-log line is the live path and the crash-report artifact is how a stall that killed the compositor actually surfaces afterwards, so a detector on either alone has a blind side. macos:unified_log currently carries the predicate feed but no watchdog line, because the only such event on this host predates the input being repaired.
search = index=os (sourcetype="macos:unified_log" OR sourcetype=macos:crashreport) "userspace watchdog timeout"
dispatch.earliest_time = -10m
dispatch.latest_time = now
cron_schedule = */5 * * * *
enableSched = 1
is_visible = 1
disabled = 0
alert.severity = 5
alert.suppress = 1
alert.suppress.period = 30m
alert.suppress.fields = host
alert.track = 1
counttype = number of events
relation = greater than
quantity = 0

[mac_kernel_panic_jetsam_arrival]
{{ alert_delivery -}}
description = Fires when a new kernel panic or JetsamEvent artifact lands in sourcetype=macos:crashreport. VERIFIED live: this sourcetype carries ~1,339 events/24h on this host, and the search below matched real .ips artifacts directly.
search = index=os sourcetype=macos:crashreport (source="*panic*" OR source="*JetsamEvent*")
dispatch.earliest_time = -10m
dispatch.latest_time = now
cron_schedule = */5 * * * *
enableSched = 1
is_visible = 1
disabled = 0
alert.severity = 5
alert.suppress = 1
alert.suppress.period = 15m
alert.suppress.fields = host
alert.track = 1
counttype = number of events
relation = greater than
quantity = 0
